      "text": [
        {
          "id": "title",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "#5→0 · A32/C55 with all three motions; A34's order of dependence; C38's recursive offices; A35; A36",
          "title": "Humanity follows the return",
          "italic": "The whole returns-to its vocation: thought's products can lead back toward the conditions of knowing instead of occupying their place — the person who follows does not merely receive a better likeness.",
          "body": "",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.05,
          "width": 560,
          "size": 30,
          "align": "left"
        },
        {
          "id": "body1",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "The person who follows the turn does not merely receive a better likeness: the relation to likeness has changed. An exteriorised measure can be used, examined, corrected, set down; the user recovers the felt comparison. The mirror keeps its place in the order of dependence: Bimba names Original, pratibimba the situated display — the Original prior in being, later in recognition; neither precedence makes the reflection ontologically Original. Native 020",
          "x": 0.04,
          "y": 0.42,
          "width": 620,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left",
          "w": 520
        },
        {
          "id": "body2",
          "visible": true,
          "kicker": "",
          "title": "",
          "italic": "",
          "body": "compares three instruments: the net binds without releasing the living parties; the attunement brings cycles to a dial unowned; the mirror adds causal recursion — capture, attunement, initiated return stay distinct offices. The institution enters the same return: exposing the measures by which it selects and judges — labour, cost, affected worlds. A35 orients compassion; A36's terminal movement: self-description alone cannot discharge Return. Occurrences: the three motions (#1–#3, #5→0).",
          "x": 0.545,
          "y": 0.42,
          "width": 570,
          "size": 14,
          "align": "left"
        }
